From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bron Gondwana <brong@fastmailteam.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:13:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] DKIM2 draft -07: From rewrite, exploded hint, unsigned
 posts start a chain

Draft -07 requires the From header field to be Authentic (section 11):
in the signing domain of the hop that set it, i=1 for the From the
message started with.  Sympa's hop always changes a list post, so on a
DKIM2 list (dkim2_message_instance on, not anonymous) dmarc_protect now
always rewrites From to the list address, whatever dmarc_protection.mode
says; ToList and DoForward shelve it.  For a signed post the original
From is in the header Recipe of the instance Sympa adds and the list
host's signature covers the new one.

A post that arrived without a DKIM2-Signature leaves the list host as
i=1, and i=1 is checked against the From of the first instance: keeping
the m=1 added at ingress (author's From) with the rewrite in m=2 fails
that check.  So egress now removes the chain for such posts, as for
anonymous lists and archive resends, and the outbound signer starts a new
one with the rewritten From.

dmarc_protection.other_email and anonymous_sender must be addresses in
the list's domain; a notice is logged when they are not Authentic for it.

Every distribution copy carries X-DKIM2-Exploded: yes (outside the
hashes as an X- field), asking the outbound signer to set f=exploded.

Requires Mail::DKIM2 0.23 (draft -07: the "u" Recipe step, From-Authentic
checks, the Exploded signer option).  DKIM2_DRAFT is now
ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-07 and DKIM2_DATE 2026-10-18.  t/DKIM2.t signs and
verifies the list host's hop with the real Mail::DKIM2 Signer/Verifier;
its fixtures now model a signed post.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
